The hourly /spawn cleanup no longer deletes the worktree of a --bg worker that is still running. It's committed as 8616ed57, and build, all tests, clippy with -D warnings and the fmt check pass.

The bug: at the start of each /spawn, yoyo removes any spawn worktree whose folder is more than an hour old, unless it holds uncommitted work. A background worker that hadn't written anything yet, or had committed everything, looked abandoned. Its worktree could be deleted while it was still working in it.

What changed:
• The spawn tracker now records each background worker's worktree path. A worktree counts as "live" while its worker's status is still Running, so it stops being protected once the worker completes or fails. A worker that panics stays Running, so its worktree is kept, which is the safe direction.
• The keep-or-remove decision is now a pure function, worktrees_to_sweep, that takes the live set as a parameter. Both sides are canonicalized, so a trailing slash, a . in the path or a symlinked path still matches. The cleanup function gathers the live paths from the tracker and passes them in.
• Worktrees holding uncommitted work are still kept, exactly as before (Day 234).

Tests:
• A table test of the decision covers: old and not live (removed, as before), old and live (kept), a different worker live, young, unreadable age, trailing slash, and . in the path.
• A symlink test checks that the two paths really are spelled differently, and that the same worktree is removed when nothing is live.
• A real-repo test drives the actual tracker: the worktree survives while its worker runs and is removed after it completes. Another test checks that a failed worker isn't live.
• Positive control, run as one mutate→test→restore command: forcing the live check to always pass made the table, symlink and real-repo tests fail by name. After restoring, everything was green.

Size cap: commands_spawn.rs is at its line cap, so I moved the existing test_cleanup_stale_worktrees into spawn_worktree.rs (adapted to the new signature, not deleted) to make room. The new tracker methods also live there, which meant making the tracker's inner field pub(crate). The file went from 4570 to 4560 lines.

Not fixed, filed before the push as #1097: a worker started by a different yoyo session in the same repo isn't in this session's tracker, so its worktree can still be removed after an hour. Folder age still isn't a real sign of activity. The issue suggests two possible fixes: a pid marker file, or an flock held by the worker.

Docs: I updated docs/src/usage/commands.md and ARCHITECTURE.md's entry for spawn_worktree.rs, keeping its old "Residue" sentence and marking it superseded. A git grep '#1057' found only code comments describing the fixed behaviour, nothing user-facing.
